## 🎬 VIDEO PRESERVATION RULES (CRITICAL!)

### ⚠️ NEVER MODIFY UPLOADED VIDEOS WITHOUT USER EXPLICIT ACTION

**CRITICAL RULE:** Once a video is uploaded, its title, description, video file, and metadata MUST remain unchanged unless the user explicitly edits them through the PostUploadEditorView or deletes the video.

### Video Upload Persistence Requirements

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Preserve video metadata and files
// When updating video metadata, ONLY update what user changed
func updateVideoMetadata(
    videoId: String,
    title: String? = nil,  // Only update if provided
    description: String? = nil,  // Only update if provided
    category: VideoCategory? = nil,  // Only update if provided
    tags: [String]? = nil  // Only update if provided
) async throws {
    // Fetch existing video first
    guard let existingVideo = try await fetchVideo(videoId: videoId) else {
        throw VideoError.notFound
    }
    
    // Only update fields that are explicitly provided
    var updates: [String: Any] = [:]
    if let title = title, title != existingVideo.title {
        updates["title"] = title
    }
    if let description = description, description != existingVideo.description {
        updates["description"] = description
    }
    // ... etc
    
    // NEVER delete or replace the video file unless user explicitly deletes video
    // NEVER change videoURL or thumbnailURL unless user explicitly replaces them
}

// ❌ WRONG: Overwriting entire video object
func updateVideo(_ video: Video) async throws {
    // This could lose data if not all fields are provided!
    try await firestore.collection("videos").document(video.id).setData(video.toDictionary())
}
```

### Video File Preservation

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Preserve video files
// When user uploads a video, save it permanently
func uploadVideo(_ videoData: Data, metadata: VideoMetadata) async throws -> Video {
    // Upload to Firebase Storage
    let videoURL = try await uploadToStorage(videoData, path: "videos/\(metadata.id).mp4")
    
    // Create video document with permanent URL
    let video = Video(
        id: metadata.id,
        title: metadata.title,
        videoURL: videoURL,  // This URL must NEVER change unless user re-uploads
        // ... other fields
    )
    
    // Save to Firestore
    try await saveVideo(video)
    
    return video
}

// ❌ WRONG: Re-uploading or replacing video files
func updateVideo(_ video: Video) async throws {
    // NEVER re-upload video file unless user explicitly replaces it
    // This would cause user to lose their original upload!
}
```

### Title and Description Preservation

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Only update what user changes
class PostUploadEditorViewModel: ObservableObject {
    @Published var title: String
    @Published var description: String
    
    init(video: Video) {
        // Preserve existing values
        self.title = video.title  // Keep original title
        self.description = video.description  // Keep original description
    }
    
    func saveChanges() async throws {
        // Only send fields that actually changed
        var updates: [String: Any] = [:]
        
        if title != video.title {
            updates["title"] = title  // Only update if changed
        }
        
        if description != video.description {
            updates["description"] = description  // Only update if changed
        }
        
        // If nothing changed, don't make any updates
        guard !updates.isEmpty else { return }
        
        try await VideoFirestoreService.shared.updateVideoMetadata(
            videoId: video.id,
            title: title != video.title ? title : nil,
            description: description != video.description ? description : nil
        )
    }
}

// ❌ WRONG: Always overwriting with current state
func saveChanges() async throws {
    // This could overwrite with empty values if user didn't change anything!
    try await updateVideo(video.id, title: title, description: description)
}
```

### Video Deletion Rules

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT: Only delete when user explicitly requests deletion
func deleteVideo(videoId: String) async throws {
    // Show confirmation dialog first
    // Only delete after user confirms
    
    // Delete from Firestore
    try await firestore.collection("videos").document(videoId).delete()
    
    // Delete from storage
    try await storage.reference(forURL: video.videoURL).delete()
    
    // Delete thumbnail
    try await storage.reference(forURL: video.thumbnailURL).delete()
}

// ❌ WRONG: Auto-deleting or replacing videos
func updateVideo(_ newVideo: Video) async throws {
    // NEVER delete old video file when updating metadata
    // User's original upload must be preserved
}
```

### Rules Summary

1. **NEVER** modify video files after upload unless user explicitly replaces them
2. **NEVER** change videoURL or thumbnailURL unless user explicitly updates them
3. **NEVER** overwrite entire video objects - only update changed fields
4. **ALWAYS** preserve original title and description unless user edits them
5. **ALWAYS** fetch existing video before updating to preserve unchanged fields
6. **ALWAYS** require explicit user action for destructive operations (delete, replace)
7. **NEVER** auto-play videos - require user to press play button
8. **NEVER** restart videos automatically - preserve playback position
9. **ALWAYS** save video metadata immediately after upload
10. **ALWAYS** increment user's videoCount after successful upload

### YouTube Parity: Video Behavior

- Videos should NOT auto-play when opened
- Videos should NOT restart when user navigates away and back
- Videos should preserve playback position when minimized to mini-player
- Mini-player should work correctly and not show error states
- Video titles should support @channel mentions and #hashtags
- Uploaded videos should persist exactly as uploaded (title, file, metadata)

